Figure  7  shows the TEM characterization results of the nanospheric precipitates in the HAZ on the CLF-1 steel side of the CLF-1/316LN-IG steels laser welded joint. Figure  7 a shows that the nanoscale, nearly spherical precipitates are distributed within grains. Figure  7 b shows the element distribution results obtained via EDS within the precipitates. These results confirm that the nanospheric precipitates are primarily enriched with Ta and C, while the surrounding matrix phase is enriched with Fe. Figure  7 c shows the high resolution TEM (HRTEM) analysis of the interface between the nanospheric precipitate and the matrix. Figure  7 d is a close-up of region 2 in Fig.  7 c and identifies the nano-precipitates as rock-salt TaC and the matrix phase as bcc α-Fe. As shown in Fig.  7 e, further fast Fourier transform (FFT) analysis confirms the observation direction along the [101] axis, with [101] TaC and [111] α-Fe exhibiting coaxial alignment. The orientation relationship between the TaC nano-precipitate and the α-Fe matrix is (020) TaC //( 01 1 ¯ \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
